WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.000
There is a sentence that can make one

2
00:00:02.060 --> 00:00:03.720
mistake last for weeks.

3
00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:05.640
I am a disaster.

4
00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:09.440
One play goes wrong, and suddenly we're

5
00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:11.160
no longer discussing what happened.

6
00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:13.760
We are talking about who we think we

7
00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:14.140
are.

8
00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:18.720
On a team I played for, we lost a game

9
00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:20.780
after a simple misunderstanding.

10
00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:24.090
Two of us expected the other to cover

11
00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:25.070
the same space.

12
00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:27.980
Afterwards, nobody wanted to watch the

13
00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:28.570
recording.

14
00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:31.740
We were all expecting a search for

15
00:00:31.750 --> 00:00:32.560
someone to blame.

16
00:00:33.560 --> 00:00:35.370
Our coach set one condition.

17
00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:38.180
First, describe what we could see

18
00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:41.580
without adjectives, who was where, which

19
00:00:41.590 --> 00:00:44.460
signal we had received, what information

20
00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:45.160
was missing.

21
00:00:46.610 --> 00:00:48.840
The conversation changed.

22
00:00:48.920 --> 00:00:50.960
We were still accountable, but now we

23
00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:51.520
could think.

24
00:00:52.310 --> 00:00:54.320
We discovered that we had rehearsed the

25
00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:56.600
play without practising how to

26
00:00:56.660 --> 00:00:59.880
communicate when the situation changed.

27
00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:02.540
We chose a clear signal and repeated it

28
00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:03.420
in training.

29
00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:07.160
We did not promise never to fail again.

30
00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:10.020
We agreed on how to prepare better.

31
00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:13.720
The same thing happens in organisations.

32
00:01:13.780 --> 00:01:16.140
A delivery is late and labels appear

33
00:01:16.220 --> 00:01:16.890
immediately.

34
00:01:17.670 --> 00:01:20.280
Poor commitment, bad attitude, lack of

35
00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:20.820
talent.

36
00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:24.020
Sometimes those words close the

37
00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:26.180
conversation before we understand the

38
00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:27.880
problem.

39
00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:30.800
At your next review, try this order:

40
00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:31.540
What happened?

41
00:01:31.640 --> 00:01:33.060
What could we control?

42
00:01:33.250 --> 00:01:35.640
And what will we practise differently?

43
00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:38.640
Finish with one action, someone

44
00:01:38.680 --> 00:01:41.140
responsible for it, and a time to check

45
00:01:41.180 --> 00:01:42.240
it.

46
00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:44.060
Confidence does not mean believing

47
00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:45.320
everything will go well.

48
00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:47.970
It means knowing that when something

49
00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:51.400
goes wrong, we can face it and prepare

50
00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:52.760
the next play together.
